{
  "sn35.89:0.1": "Linked Discourses 35.89 ",
  "sn35.89:0.2": "9. With Channa ",
  "sn35.89:0.3": "With Bāhiya ",
  "sn35.89:1.1": "Then Venerable Bāhiya went up to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him: ",
  "sn35.89:1.2": "“Sir, may the Buddha please teach me Dhamma in brief. When I’ve heard it, I’ll live alone, withdrawn, diligent, keen, and resolute.” ",
  "sn35.89:2.1": "“What do you think, Bāhiya? ",
  "sn35.89:2.2": "Is the eye permanent or impermanent?” ",
  "sn35.89:3.1": "“Impermanent, sir.” ",
  "sn35.89:4.1": "“But if it’s impermanent, is it suffering or happiness?” ",
  "sn35.89:5.1": "“Suffering, sir.” ",
  "sn35.89:6.1": "“But if it’s impermanent, suffering, and perishable, is it fit to be regarded thus: ",
  "sn35.89:6.2": "‘This is mine, I am this, this is my self’?” ",
  "sn35.89:7.1": "“No, sir.” ",
  "sn35.89:8.1": "“Are sights … ",
  "sn35.89:9.1": "",
  "sn35.89:9.2": "eye consciousness … ",
  "sn35.89:9.3": "eye contact … ",
  "sn35.89:9.4": "The pleasant, painful, or neutral feeling that arises dependent on mind contact: is that permanent or impermanent?” ",
  "sn35.89:10.1": "“Impermanent, sir.” ",
  "sn35.89:11.1": "“But if it’s impermanent, is it suffering or happiness?” ",
  "sn35.89:12.1": "“Suffering, sir.” ",
  "sn35.89:13.1": "“But if it’s impermanent, suffering, and perishable, is it fit to be regarded thus: ",
  "sn35.89:13.2": "‘This is mine, I am this, this is my self’?” ",
  "sn